# Asaas payment conventions

Asaas moves real money. Security- and sandbox-first.

- API key comes from config (`config('services.asaas.key')`), never hardcoded, never in logs/tests/client. Separate sandbox and production keys.
- Base URL from config keyed on environment; default to sandbox (`https://sandbox.asaas.com/api/`), production opt-in. Build/test in sandbox first.
- Auth is the `access_token` header, not Bearer. Use Laravel's `Http` client; don't add an SDK unless one is already installed.
- Don't handle raw card data (PCI-DSS): prefer tokenization or hosted checkout. Confirm before accepting card fields.
- Verify every webhook's auth token against `config('services.asaas.webhook_token')`; reject on mismatch. Process idempotently on a queue and respond 200 fast.
- Trust the gateway (responses/webhooks), not the client, for amounts and paid status. Send idempotency keys on creation.
- Never log secrets or PII; log the Asaas `id` + status only.
- Tests first (per `tdd`): fake `Http`, cover valid/invalid webhook token, idempotent duplicate delivery, and refund/cancel transitions. Never hit the live API in CI.

